# Introducing Risk Analysis and Calculation of Profitability under Uncertainty in Engineering Design

**Authors:** Kosmopoulou, Georgia, Freeman, Margaret, Papavassiliou, Dimitrios V.

## Abstract
A major challenge that chemical engineering graduates face at the modern workplace is the management and operation of plants under conditions of uncertainty. Developments in the fields of industrial organization and microeconomics offer tools to address this challenge with rather well developed concepts, such as decision theory and financial risk analysis. In this work we discuss the development and implementation of assignments that utilize the concepts of risk and uncertainty and the use of software to incorporate financial risk in engineering economics.

